# Modjam — Allowed Dependencies & References

## Allowed dependencies

Use these frameworks as the primary modding stack. Prefer their abstractions over direct game assembly bindings.

| Package | Docs | Purpose |
|---------|------|---------|
| **S1API** | https://ifbars.github.io/S1API/index.html | Cross-compatible Schedule One modding (Mono + IL2CPP): NPCs, quests, items, phone apps, save data, lifecycle hooks |
| **S1MAPI** | https://ifbars.github.io/S1MAPI/index.html | Procedural geometry, building system, runtime GLTF/GLB loading |

Do not introduce other third-party modding frameworks unless the user explicitly approves them.

## Reference mods (implementation only)

The user’s prior mods live at `D:\Vibecoded\ScheduleOne\`. You may read their source for patterns and implementation ideas:

- `More-NPCs`
- `S1-Thors-Hammer`
- `WeaponShipments`

**Brainstorming:** Do **not** use these mods as inspiration when ideating features, themes, or scope. Treat them as code references only after direction is set.

**Implementation:** When building, match conventions found in those projects (project layout, S1API usage, build setup) where appropriate.
